## Complete scalar problem

For every degree-21 ternary form `S`, let

```text
C_S : K_6 -> Sym^15
```

be its `(6,15)` catalecticant.  The source space `Sym^21` has dimension 253.
Projecting the image modulo the selected primitive plane gives a linear
obstruction on all 253 scalar sources at once.

At every one of the 48 archived split fibers, under both divided-power and
ordinary differentiation, the obstruction has profile

```text
rank 244, nullity 9.
```

The same nine source monomials span the nullspace at every fiber.  Their
catalecticants vanish identically on `K_6`, so every admissible scalar source
induces rank zero.  No nonzero scalar degree-21 catalecticant reaches the
selected primitive plane.

## Consequence

This strictly contains and retires the raw `A_theta*K_6` and 33-source tests
from UST.G3FY.  Collecting more scalar factors or scalar transvectants cannot
solve the bridge.  The missing compiler must be non-Hankel and matrix-valued,
with the derived data already visible in the selected Griffiths--Dwork chain:

```text
Jacobian division
  -> original-partial correction
  -> minus-divergence return
  -> H02 normal projection.
```

The immediate target is to apply that frozen chain to all 18 source vectors
and compare its `136 x 18` image with the selected primitive plane.

## Boundary

The theorem is exact at all 48 archived finite fibers.  It does not promote
the target plane to `Q(gamma)`, exclude matrix-valued derived operators, close
component 20 over characteristic zero, or establish a physical endpoint.

